## By region

table region title="p95 latency, ms"

## What we learned

- Shard count matters more than shard size
-- Going from 24 to 40 shards removed the hot spots
-- Shards above 60 GB still need a split
- Warm the cache before shifting traffic
- The ap-south regression is a network issue, not an index issue

### Do
- Rebuild one region at a time
- Keep the old index for 48 hours

### Avoid
- Rebuilding during the weekly batch window
- Shifting more than 20% of traffic per step

## Next steps

1. Add ap-south to the cross-region peering review.
2. Raise the cache warm-up budget from 10 to 25 minutes.
3. Re-run this review after the November rebuild.
